# FormSy candidate audit of execution evidence

Review the supplied evidence independently. Scope can cover a single condition,
and the document modules are optional for this audit.
TraceAudit uses release `traceaudit-r12`, interpretation revision `1.9.1`,
machine contract `1.9`, and candidate report schema
`traceaudit-candidate-0.1`. The document modules use their separate
`formsy-sop-contract-0.2`.

## Bind the sources and available capabilities

Read the [candidate report contract](references/候选报告约定.md) and the
[r12 reading guide](references/traceaudit-r12-reading-guide.md). Run
`python3 scripts/validate_traceaudit.py` to verify the nine manifest entries
and the 33 rules, 144 conditions, and 184 atomic obligations. Record the
execution gap if Python is unavailable. The ten r12 files retain their
original bytes. The r11 material remains available for historical review.
Treat external relative links and upstream commands in those records as
provenance.

Keep `reference_only=true` and `source_authenticated=false`. Establish the
actual user task, target version, effective requirements, readable input
extent, and rules cited for this round. For historical work with an unknown
original rule set, label the result as retrospective reference analysis.
Obtain current authorization and confirmation from actual user decisions.
Record source requirements, assistant claims, tool observations, and current
inferences separately. Verify quotation accuracy, semantic support, version
binding, and source identity independently.

## Select scope and read the applicable rules

Freeze the `code_fix` or `full_sop` profile before seeing results. Use
`code_fix` for a draft when the scope is unspecified, and disclose the
choice. Read [interpretation sections 0–5](references/traceaudit-r12-reading-guide.md#0-freeze-the-audit-profile-and-triggers).
Use the [compiled catalog](references/traceaudit-r12/compiled-catalog.json)
to locate each selected rule's parent clause, conditions, all atomic
obligations, dimensions, triggers, and gates. Check the actual technical,
security, or code-fix source. Use `coverage_manifest` to identify the material
outside compiled coverage.

- For `code_fix`, cover every substantive diff and the calls, data, and
  side effects needed to assess it. Derive `design_full`, `formal_closure`,
  and `full_security` from the original user and assistant material.
  Record uncertain evidence or meaning as `uncertain` and restore the
  corresponding full check. Defer an item only when supported as
  `not_requested`. Keep deferred items `unverified` in the original matrix.
  The SEC10 release and update identity obligation remains in scope even
  when product governance is deferred.
- For `full_sop`, assess the complete original SOP for applicability and
  evaluate each condition within the available capability and evidence.
  Deliver a partial candidate with the unreviewed scope when inputs are incomplete.
- Record missing source identity, program gates, frozen quotations,
  independent stage reviews, or runtime adapters. Keep affected definitive
  conclusions `unverified`. Describe the stages actually executed.

## Review and deliver

1. Separate mandatory acceptance, requested fixes, compatibility constraints,
   observations, diagnosis, and workarounds in the original request. Combine
   identical triggers and expectations when appropriate. Attribute chosen
   implementation details to their actual source. Retain frozen originals
   and versions. Under interpretation revision 1.9.1, distinguish effective
   new requirements, old test assertions, and explicit test deliverables.
   Keep unresolved conflicts between effective requirements `unverified`.
2. Review every atomic obligation under each selected condition. Distinguish
   design, implementation, test delivery, actual execution, and closure
   evidence. Use `unverified` for missing evidence. Use `unsatisfied` only
   with a direct counterexample for the same condition, object, task,
   version, and dimension. Require affirmative exclusion evidence for
   `not_applicable`. Apply conjunctive obligations with `all` and retain
   independent parent gates. Propagate failure only where the corresponding
   obligation applies.
3. For TC14, bind the exact assistant statement and context to its
   proposition, modality, object, property, and version. Compare that with
   independent sources. Classify plans, user wishes, and tool output by
   what they actually support. Evidence reuse can occur within one task.
   Distinguish task evidence from the product's external input capabilities.
   Record any gaps in coverage of assistant statements or properties.
4. Cite each source's own revision, task and target binding, precise line
   range, and verbatim text from the material read. Check sufficient context
   for whole-file absence, conflicting contracts, and initialization causes.
   Compare parent and target versions independently. Limit test conclusions
   to the actual coverage. For SEC06, identify the credential object and
   version in the audited project, dependency, or build. Track credentials
   used by the audit tool separately. Distinguish a credential reference
   from observed exposure or verified protection. Treat runtime identity as
   a separate evidence requirement.
5. Deliver the candidate report, unverified, excluded and unreviewed scope,
   analysis failures, and known residuals. Group findings by a supported
   common cause while retaining every original condition and citation.
   Report the groups as candidates. Preserve old reports, failures, and
   inputs. Record decisions, revisions, retests, and formal closure
   separately. Keep `formal_closed=false` in every candidate report.

For a machine-readable file, use the [candidate template](assets/candidate-audit.template.json)
and run `python3 scripts/validate_traceaudit.py /absolute/path/candidate-audit.json`.
The validator verifies frozen bytes, registered structure, and the locations
of quotations in supplied text. Verify semantic support, input completeness,
identity, and historical execution independently. Send document revision
findings and version impacts to the relevant product, technical, or
knowledge module and recheck with selfcheck. Use the candidate report schema
for this output.

## Retain limits and residuals

Preserve the known TC14, SEC06, TC13, FIX03/FIX04, and TC04/TC05 residuals
in r12. For historical test records, use the frozen sources linked by the
r12 reading guide. A full evaluation requires the applicable input,
actual execution, and independent review.

This module reads supplied material and can run the local structural validator.
Handle external trace retrieval, paid model calls, business execution,
deployment, or formal closure through a separately authorized workflow. If
material, access, or budget is missing, retain the completed portion and the
stop point. Clarify decisions that change requirements, authorization, or user
confirmation with the current user.
